# EtherPK Client settings.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for `pnpm dev`, or pass the same names to the Docker image or the Node
# bundle's environment. A line that starts `# NAME=` is optional: uncomment it to use it. Nothing
# here is required: with every setting unset the Client runs local graphs and offers a Custom
# server form for connecting to a Sync Server by its address.
#
# See https://docs.etherpk.com/running-etherpk-on-your-own-computer

# --- Custom server ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A Sync Server address the Custom server form starts filled in with.
# PUBLIC_CUSTOM_SYNC_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- Spell check -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where dictionaries are downloaded from: the folder holding `manifest.json`. Unset uses
# https://dictionaries.etherpk.com/v1; an empty value turns dictionary downloads off.
# PUBLIC_DICTIONARY_URL=https://dictionaries.example.com/v1

# --- Legal pages -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Terms and Privacy Policy, linked from the footer of the Client's public pages. Leave them
# unset to link none.
# PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://example.com/terms
# PUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://example.com/privacy

# --- Network ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the Node server listens. The Docker image sets PORT=3000.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# Behind a reverse proxy or CDN: the header that carries the visitor's address, which the request
# log records. Unset, the log shows the proxy's address. The proxy must overwrite this header and
# be the only way to reach the Client, or anyone can put a false address in the log. For example,
# `X-Real-IP` behind nginx with `proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;`, or `CF-Connecting-IP`
# behind Cloudflare.
# ADDRESS_HEADER=X-Real-IP
# With ADDRESS_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For: the number of proxies in front of the Client.
# XFF_DEPTH=1

# --- Logging ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `debug`, `info` (the default), `warn` or `error`. Logs go to stdout as JSON.
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# Also send logs to an OpenObserve ingestion endpoint, with the Authorization header value it needs.
# OPENOBSERVE_URL=
# OPENOBSERVE_AUTH=
